				<p class="text-lg text-vg-gray-dark text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-10">
					The hardest part of adopting agentic development isn't the technology. It's the shift in how developers work.
				</p>

				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-vg-burgundy">What changes for developers</h3>
						<ul class="space-y-3 text-vg-gray-dark">
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="arrow-right" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>Less time writing code line by line, more time specifying what to build and reviewing what AI produces</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="arrow-right" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>Stronger emphasis on testing as a design tool, not just a verification step</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="arrow-right" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>More focus on clear specifications and domain modeling up front</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="arrow-right" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>Working at a higher level of abstraction, like every previous shift in programming languages</span>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-vg-burgundy">Why embedded works for this</h3>
						<ul class="space-y-3 text-vg-gray-dark">
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="check" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>People learn new practices by doing, not by reading a recommendations document</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="check" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>Pairing with someone who already works this way is the fastest path to adoption</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="check" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>Resistance fades when people experience the results firsthand on their own codebase</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
								<span class="text-vg-red mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
									<Icon name="check" size="sm" />
								</span>
								<span>The new practices become self-reinforcing once the team sees the productivity difference</span>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
